2026-10-19T22:24:27.0814013Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 57217
2026-10-19T22:24:27.0814333Z   ISSUE_TITLE: [FEATURE]: Plugin API: let a plugin run its tool transform last
2026-10-19T22:24:27.0818569Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Problem

Tool transforms run in registration order. A plugin that adds its transform after a different plugin can replace a tool. The replacement discards the wrapper that an earlier plugin added. A plugin cannot select the last position for its transform.

## Source (v2.0.31)

- `packages/core/src/state.ts:19` gives the order:

  `Registers a scoped transform. Reads rebuild by applying every registered transform in order.`
- `packages/core/src/state.ts:178` applies the transforms in insertion order:

  `for (const transform of transforms) {`
- `packages/core/src/tool/AGENTS.md:37` shows that the tool registry uses this state:

  `The service uses shared State to replay synchronous transforms in registration order against a fresh editor.`

## Purpose

A credential-filter plugin adds a wrapper to all tools. The wrapper removes secrets from tool output. A plugin that adds its transform after a different plugin replaces one tool with its own definition. The replacement has no wrapper. The secret filter stops for that tool.

## Proposed minimal API

Add an order option to `ctx.tool.transform`. A plugin with the last order runs after all other transforms.

## What the plugin does today without it

The plugin cannot control the order. The plugin must add its transform again after all other plugins, and the order is not stable.

